I've pieced my information on monster spellcasting behavour together
from the guidebook, combined with the following sources:

Kate Nepveu's Elbereth FAQ
http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/elbereth_faq.html

Kate Nepveu's Demogorgon FAQ
www.steelypips.org/nethack/demogorgon_faq.html

David Corbett's Monster Spell Spoiler
http://www.geocities.com/dcorbett42/nethack/monspell.htm

The devteam was quite specific:  "Engraving the word ``Elbereth'' will
cause most monsters to not attack you hand-to-hand ..."  No mention of
spellcasting and Elbereth is made here, darn.

Sadly, neither Kate Nepveu's Elbereth FAQ nor David Corbett's Monster
Spell Spoiler discuss what effects (if any) Elbereth has on monster
spellcasting.

The only clue I dug up was from the Kate Nepveu's Demogorgon FAQ:
"Once you're on the up stairs with Elbereth inscribed, you can pound on
Demogorgon freely while he can only cast spells at you from the next
square."  No discussion was made of what spells he would and wouldn't
cast.

Unfortunately, I'm not familiar enough with the relavant portions of
the source code to do anything other than get lost in a twisty little
maze of functions.

My innate paranoia (w.r.t. nethack malice) combined with these sources
led me to believe that the E-word imposed no limitations on monster
spellcasting.

